3 eggs / omelet * 7 omelets / week * 4 weeks = 84 eggs. 84 eggs / 12 eggs / dozen = 7 dozens.

Claire eats 84 eggs in 4 weeks. To find out how many dozens of eggs that is, we divide the total number of eggs by the number of eggs in a dozen (12). So, 84 eggs / 12 eggs/dozen = 7 dozens.

\boxed{7}

